It is the afternoon.
It is my lunch break.
I go outside the office.
There is a mobile shop nearby.
I go inside the shop.
There is a man in the shop.
I call him 'bhaiya'.
"Namaste bhaiya," I say.
"Namaste madam," bhaiya says.
"I want a new SIM card," I explain.
"I do not have an Indian SIM card."
"I only have a Mexico number."
"No problem madam," he says.
"Do you have your passport?" he asks.
"Yes, I have my passport," I say.
I take out my passport from the bag.
"Okay madam," bhaiya says.
He takes out a tablet.
Getting a new SIM card is very easy.
